BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-20261030-14@tonight
DTSTAMP:20261026T104104Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T203000
SUMMARY:Natalie Brooke & Matt Jalbert Band
LOCATION:Bowery Palace\, East Village
DESCRIPTION:Natalie Brooke is a rock star. A virtuoso funk / rock keys play
 
er leading her powerhouse 4-piece band from the Baltimore area. The explosi
 
ve act is fronted by Natalie on keys\, synth\, keytar\, and vocals and back
 
ed by drummer Nathan Shulkin\, Nester on the bass\, and Luke Walker on the 
 
guitar. She kicks off every show with a punch and never lets the energy dro
 
p - audiences move\, dance\, scream\, jump\, and ride the wild wave of the 
 
set with her and the band. Natalie's music was once said to be a mashup of 
 
Rick James and Rush. She has an undeniably infectious vibe featuring a fier
 
y blend of fast tempos and sloshy rock elements balanced with her transcend
 
ent jazz and classical roots. Natalie brings an exceptionally unique approa
 
ch to the keyboard that is equally percussive and melodic that lights up th
 
e show with every electrifying note she plays. She is on a meteoric rise\, 
 
frequently sharing the stage with pillars of the rock\, funk\, and jazz sce
 
nes. Pigeons Playing Ping Pong\, Andy Frasco & the UN\, Dogs in a Pile\, Ka
 
nika Moore\, Big Something\, Cris Jacobs\, Doom Flamingo\, Sunsquabi\, lesp
 
ecial\, and the Magic Beans are a few of the artists Natalie has played wit
 
h recently. Matt Jalbert Band is the new song-driven project from guitarist
 
 and founding member of TAUK. After more than a decade of touring nationall
 
y with TAUK---including appearances at Bonnaroo and Hulaween and performanc
 
es at venues like Red Rocks Amphitheatre---Jalbert steps forward as a lead 
 
vocalist and songwriter\, bringing a new dimension to his sound. Blending g
 
roove-forward indie rock with psychedelic and blues influences\, Matt Jalbe
 
rt Band pairs deep-pocket grooves and adventurous musicianship with concise
 
\, melodic\, and lyrical songs. The lineup features Matt Jalbert (guitar/vo
 
cals)\, Ben Atkind (drums)\, Eli Winderman (keys/vocals)\, Jonathan Colman 
 
(bass)\, and Adam November (guitar). The album\, Somebody's Child\, arrives
 
 November 20\, with the title track and first single dropping September 18.
 
 Following Jalbert's 2025 instrumental solo release Sauce Buffet\, Somebody
 
's Child marks a new chapter---pairing his signature guitar work and groove
 
 with vocals\, melody\, and a more direct emotional voice. Tickets & info: 
 
https://www.ticketweb.com/event/natalie-brooke-matt-jalbert-bowery-palace-t
 
ickets/15038133
URL:https://www.ticketweb.com/event/natalie-brooke-matt-jalbert-bowery-pala
 
ce-tickets/15038133
END:VEVENT
